      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Considering world instance createor is owner if the world with the map (it essentially a server on it's own) which already have moderation rights on that world (can warn and kick), banning people from using map will only create needless issues when people want to join each other (some people would say that private worlds alone already creates those problems). And trust me, everyone knows that there would be unjustified map bans, im too long on internet to not predict that. \n\nNot to mention you always have option to keep your map not public where you always be world owner and have moderation rights on it, i know some people aspecially on Japanese side of community that does that.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
